; SPDX-License-Identifier: AGPL-3.0-only
;
; Arcen Pier SELinux policy module (CIL). Installed by install-arcen-pier
; with `semodule -i arcen.cil` only on a host with SELinux enabled; removed
; with `semodule -r arcen` on uninstall. Rationale and review notes:
; docs/security/linux-selinux.md.
;
; The packaged Pier is a systemd service, so it and its session launcher run
; as unconfined_service_t. The launcher opens each desktop through the PAM
; `login` stack, whose `pam_selinux open` assigns the session user's default
; context (unconfined_u:unconfined_r:unconfined_t for the default login
; mapping). The launcher applies that context only to the session user's
; first process, as a display manager's session worker does; the targeted
; policy lets display managers (xdm_t), sshd and init make that transition,
; but not unconfined_service_t. This is the one rule that adds.
;
; It grants no access the source domain lacks: unconfined_service_t is
; already unconfined. Confined SELinux users (user_u, staff_u, ...) are not
; added; their sessions are refused by the launcher with a clear error.
(allow unconfined_service_t unconfined_t (process (transition)))
